.TH PATINA-GREETER 1 "2026-10-19" "patina-desktop 0.1.0" "Patina Desktop"
.SH NAME
patina-greeter \- Patina sign-in screen for greetd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patina-compositor \-\-greeter patina-greeter
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patina-greeter
is the Patina sign-in screen for the
.BR greetd (1)
login daemon. It shows the time, the people who can sign in (accounts with a login shell and
a user id from 1000), and a password field; it checks the password through greetd and starts
.B patina-session
for the user. The button bottom-left picks another user; the one bottom-right shuts the
computer down.
.PP
It runs inside its own compositor:
.B patina-compositor \-\-greeter
starts it and ends when it ends. An example greetd configuration is in
.IR /usr/share/doc/patina-desktop/greetd-config.toml .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATINA_GREETER_SESSION
The command started for the user instead of
.BR patina-session .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patina-session (1),
.BR patina-lock (1)
